# Example crontab for the paper trader. Copy, adjust paths, then install with `crontab -e`.
# Keys and the webhook are read from the environment or a file you source yourself;
# do not put them in this file.
# The schedule fires every fifteen minutes in the machine's time zone; `trader run --if-due`
# decides whether a run is due, using America/New_York market time, so no CRON_TZ is needed.
*/15 * * * * /usr/local/bin/trader run --if-due >> "$HOME/paper-trader/run.log" 2>&1
